{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "SCENE-CORE-001-R2",
  "title": "Scene boundaries and progressive Skills with independent optional cognition",
  "requirements": [
    "Canonical scene policy rejects mismatched scope and preserves group allowlists and the private switch",
    "Skill directory, always-on text, selection and explicit loading filter group/private before budgets; missing audience stays group-only",
    "Owner skill declarations support a closed explicit audience and cannot bypass scene restrictions",
    "Group and private cognitive routes select independently and private never inherits the historical group graph",
    "Private tools are authorized for the peer only and group-only operations remain hidden and denied",
    "Private lifecycle is independent of group ambient admission; direct group prompt and all legacy behavior regressions remain valid",
    "Public extension surface remains instruction Skills and task definitions; no runtime tool or graph plugin interface is added",
    "Disabled private channels deny tools even for a canonical peer"
  ],
